    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe following shows the recommended indentation:\n```python\n\"[\"\n#\n```\n```python\nb\"abc\"\n#\n```\n```python\nf\"[\"\n#\n```\n```python\nr\"[\"\n#\n```\n```python\nb\"[\"\n    #\n```\n```python\nb\"[\"\n    b\"]\"\n#\n```\n\nIt appears that nvim thinks opening braces inside of b strings are actual opening braces which causes the indentation.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee examples\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAll of the examples above should never be indented.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.4 (commit unknown)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes, 9.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch linux 7.1.4.arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nArch pacman extra repository",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
